<title>USA: U.S. auto CEOs' Friday Clinton meeting postponed.</title>
<headline>U.S. auto CEOs' Friday Clinton meeting postponed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>A meeting between President Clinton and the top executives of the Big Three U.S. carmakers that was planned for Friday has been postponed, an industry source said Thursday.</p>
<p>The meeting was put off because United Auto Workers union President Stephen Yokich, who was to be a part of the discussions, was unable to attend Friday's session, the source said. It is expected to be rescheduled for mid-July, he said.</p>
<p>The executives were expected to discuss trade and environmental issues with the president.</p>
</text>
